      "side": 1,
      "message": "these calls are not ubsan safe. You are passing integer values to a function expecting an enum.\n\nAlso, how do other kernel tracepoint print enums? Is there a better way to automate this enum to string translation then adding functions that we manually have to keep in sync? (See __print_symbolic for how at least some other trace points print enums)",
      "revId": "b653a72d5b22ac3e36a183293317939c40bb9012",
